      "content": "ACE inhibitors can cause several clinical side effects, but one of the most notable is a dry, hacking cough, also known as a persistent cough. This is primarily due to the accumulation of bradykinin, a potent vasodilator, in the lungs. When ACE is inhibited, bradykinin is not broken down as quickly, and its increased levels in the lungs cause an inflammatory response, leading to coughing.",
